1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,978
Ava: A training job that moves to another accelerator with a small change gives a team more choices.
Ava：只需小幅改动就能把训练任务迁到另一种加速器，团队就有了更多选择。

2
00:00:06,978 --> 00:00:12,487
Then performance tuning begins, and shapes or sharding may still need work.
接下来还要调优性能，张量形状和分片方式可能仍需调整。

3
00:00:12,487 --> 00:00:18,566
That gap runs through the PyTorch Conference North America 2026 announcements.
这种差距贯穿了 2026 年北美 PyTorch 大会的各项发布。

4
00:00:18,566 --> 00:00:24,267
Brian: The event brought at least 3,500 attendees to San Jose on October 20 and 21.
Brian：大会于 10 月 20 日至 21 日在圣何塞举行，吸引了至少 3,500 人参加。

5
00:00:24,267 --> 00:00:28,318
Its theme was accelerating open intelligence together.
大会主题是“携手加速开放智能”。

6
00:00:28,318 --> 00:00:38,044
For framework engineers, the interesting part is how work on training, serving, compilers, hardware, and production connects.
对框架工程师来说，值得关注的是训练、推理服务、编译器、硬件和生产环境如何衔接。

7
00:00:38,044 --> 00:00:45,329
Ava: Mark Collier set out a goal of training and serving models on any chip, in any cloud, for any agent.
Ava：Mark Collier 提出的目标是：在任何芯片、任何云上，为任何智能体训练模型并提供推理服务。

8
00:00:45,329 --> 00:00:47,587
That spans a lot of boundaries.
这跨越了许多技术边界。

9
00:00:47,587 --> 00:00:54,930
A backend can open a path to new hardware, while the rest of the workload still needs attention.
后端能打通新硬件的使用路径，但工作负载的其他部分仍需处理。

10
00:00:54,930 --> 00:01:01,712
Brian: The conference connected research, models, frameworks, infrastructure, hardware, and production.
Brian：大会把研究、模型、框架、基础设施、硬件和生产环境联系了起来。

11
00:01:01,712 --> 00:01:05,526
Its announcements show several ways those layers meet.
各项发布展示了这些层面衔接的几种方式。

12
00:01:05,526 --> 00:01:10,260
Native backends support familiar PyTorch workflows on more devices.
原生后端让熟悉的 PyTorch 工作流程可以在更多设备上运行。

13
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:14,286
Compiler projects translate work for particular hardware.
编译器项目则将程序转换为适合特定硬件运行的形式。

14
00:01:14,286 --> 00:01:19,016
Other projects address training, data loading, and deployment.
其他项目涉及训练、数据加载和部署。

15
00:01:19,016 --> 00:01:21,259
Ava: Let's take a concrete workload.
Ava：来看一个具体的工作负载。

16
00:01:21,259 --> 00:01:26,325
A team trains a model in PyTorch and wants to try another accelerator.
一个团队用 PyTorch 训练模型，想试试另一种加速器。

17
00:01:26,325 --> 00:01:33,416
I'd check whether it runs, whether distributed training still fits, and what serving will require.
我会检查它能否运行、分布式训练是否仍然适用，以及推理服务需要什么。

18
00:01:33,416 --> 00:01:38,542
TorchTPU offers a path for the Google TPU part of that experiment.
TorchTPU 为这项实验中的 Google TPU 提供了一条路径。

19
00:01:38,542 --> 00:01:43,658
Brian: TorchTPU is an open source collaboration between Google and Meta.
Brian：TorchTPU 是 Google 与 Meta 合作的开源项目。

20
00:01:43,658 --> 00:01:51,766
It introduces a native PyTorch backend for Google TPUs, with eager execution and torch.compile support.
它为 Google TPU 引入原生 PyTorch 后端，支持即时执行和 torch.compile。

21
00:01:51,766 --> 00:02:03,372
The validated integrations named in the announcement include TorchTitan for training, vLLM and SGLang for inference, and Ray for orchestration.
公告列出的已验证集成包括用于训练的 TorchTitan、用于推理的 vLLM 和 SGLang，以及用于编排的 Ray。

22
00:02:03,372 --> 00:02:08,240
Ava: The caveat is that migration and peak performance are different steps.
Ava：但迁移成功和达到最佳性能是两个不同阶段。

23
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:17,699
A device change may be enough to move a workload, but reaching peak performance may require changes to shapes, sharding, and operations.
更换设备或许足以迁移工作负载，但要达到最佳性能，可能还得调整张量形状、分片方式和算子。

24
00:02:17,699 --> 00:02:23,474
I'd treat the device change as the start of an evaluation, not its conclusion.
我会把更换设备视为评估的起点，而不是终点。

25
00:02:23,474 --> 00:02:27,270
Brian: TorchNeuron makes a related move for AWS Trainium.
Brian：TorchNeuron 为 AWS Trainium 提供了类似的路径。

26
00:02:27,270 --> 00:02:30,535
It's an open source native PyTorch backend.
它是一个开源的原生 PyTorch 后端。

27
00:02:30,535 --> 00:02:38,280
The announcement says researchers can experiment and run workloads with a single configuration change.
公告称，研究人员只需更改一项配置，就能开展实验并运行工作负载。

28
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:44,248
Its public beta launched at the conference on October 20 under Apache 2.0.
它于 10 月 20 日大会期间启动公测，采用 Apache 2.0 许可证。

29
00:02:44,248 --> 00:02:50,271
Ava: Once that workload starts running, I'd look beyond the initial device change.
Ava：工作负载开始运行后，我会继续查看更换设备之外的情况。

30
00:02:50,271 --> 00:02:54,183
Training may use compilation and distributed APIs.
训练可能会用到编译和分布式 API。

31
00:02:54,183 --> 00:03:01,379
The TorchNeuron update names eager execution, torch.compile, DTensor, and torch.distributed.
TorchNeuron 的更新提到了即时执行、torch.compile、DTensor 和 torch.distributed。

32
00:03:01,379 --> 00:03:07,518
That covers more than a device switch, at least in the described workflow.
至少在所描述的工作流程中，它涵盖的不只是设备切换。

33
00:03:07,518 --> 00:03:15,551
Brian: It also names libraries such as TorchTitan and describes a path from research experimentation to production deployment.
Brian：它还提到了 TorchTitan 等库，并描述了从研究实验走向生产部署的路径。

34
00:03:15,551 --> 00:03:23,922
For a real training job, I'd check its operations and distributed setup on Trainium, then measure the behavior I care about.
对于实际训练任务，我会检查它的算子和分布式配置在 Trainium 上的表现，再测量我关心的指标。

35
00:03:23,922 --> 00:03:28,052
The configuration claim alone doesn't predict its speed.
仅凭更改配置的说法，无法预测它的速度。

36
00:03:28,052 --> 00:03:31,863
Ava: There's another boundary after a model reaches a backend.
Ava：模型适配后端之后，还要跨过另一道关。

37
00:03:31,863 --> 00:03:38,414
The device needs an executable program that follows its rules for placing tensors and moving data.
设备需要可执行的程序，而且程序必须遵循其张量放置和数据移动规则。

38
00:03:38,414 --> 00:03:41,823
That makes the IBM Spyre compiler work interesting.
这正是 IBM Spyre 编译器工作的有趣之处。

39
00:03:41,823 --> 00:03:46,786
It starts from decisions Inductor has already made about the program.
它从 Inductor 已经做出的程序决策出发。

40
00:03:46,786 --> 00:03:55,105
Brian: IBM's torch-spyre translates Inductor's decisions about work division and tensor placement into executable programs.
Brian：IBM 的 torch-spyre 将 Inductor 对任务划分和张量放置的决策转化为可执行程序。

41
00:03:55,105 --> 00:04:01,202
An open source Dataflow Scheduler builds pipelines for data movement and computation.
开源的 Dataflow Scheduler 为数据移动和计算构建流水线。

42
00:04:01,202 --> 00:04:04,501
Device-specific stages then produce SpyreCode.
随后，针对设备的编译阶段生成 SpyreCode。

43
00:04:04,501 --> 00:04:11,664
You can see how general compiler decisions become work that this particular device can execute.
由此可以看到，通用的编译器决策如何变成这款设备能够执行的程序。

44
00:04:11,664 --> 00:04:19,255
Ava: Data movement belongs in that explanation because compute alone doesn't describe the whole program.
Ava：这里必须谈到数据移动，因为仅看计算无法说明整个程序。

45
00:04:19,255 --> 00:04:24,393
The FlyDSL update takes a different route on AMD MI350-series GPUs.
FlyDSL 的更新在 AMD MI350 系列 GPU 上采取了另一条路线。

46
00:04:24,393 --> 00:04:32,138
Its optional backend connects eligible operations to optimized kernels through existing PyTorch APIs.
它的可选后端通过现有 PyTorch API，将符合条件的算子接入优化内核。

47
00:04:32,138 --> 00:04:36,782
I'd want to know what happens outside that eligible set.
我还想知道不符合条件的算子会怎样运行。

48
00:04:36,782 --> 00:04:40,788
Brian: Unsupported workloads keep their existing implementations.
Brian：不支持的工作负载仍使用原有实现。

49
00:04:40,788 --> 00:04:48,456
So the new path can apply where an operation is eligible, while other work continues through the existing path.
因此，符合条件的算子可以走新路径，其他部分继续走原有路径。

50
00:04:48,456 --> 00:04:58,684
That matters when evaluating a model with many operations: support for one optimized kernel doesn't describe the behavior of the full workload.
评估包含大量算子的模型时，这一点很重要：支持某个优化内核，并不能说明整个工作负载的表现。

51
00:04:58,684 --> 00:05:02,371
Ava: Let's follow that through to a large training workload.
Ava：我们接着看大型训练任务。

52
00:05:02,371 --> 00:05:10,417
TorchTitan expanded model support across its 5D parallelism stack and introduced reinforcement learning through TitanRL.
TorchTitan 扩展了五维并行体系支持的模型，并通过 TitanRL 引入强化学习。

53
00:05:10,417 --> 00:05:19,818
I'm interested in the boundary between training a model and running it for generation, because both activities appear in that workflow.
我想了解模型训练和生成推理之间的界限，因为这个流程两者都有。

54
00:05:19,818 --> 00:05:27,303
Brian: TitanRL keeps the same model implementation across pretraining, post-training, and execution inside vLLM.
Brian：TitanRL 在预训练、后训练和 vLLM 执行阶段复用同一套模型实现。

55
00:05:27,303 --> 00:05:33,576
That can reduce the need to maintain separate model implementations across those stages.
这能减少为各阶段分别维护模型实现的工作。

56
00:05:33,576 --> 00:05:41,696
The design also includes asynchronous rollouts and multiple forms of parallelism for training and generation.
这一设计还包括异步采样轨迹，以及用于训练和生成的多种并行方式。

57
00:05:41,696 --> 00:05:45,964
Ava: Sharing the implementation addresses one kind of duplication.
Ava：共用模型实现解决了一种重复劳动。

58
00:05:45,964 --> 00:05:53,522
Reinforcement learning also has a scheduling problem: generation produces rollouts while training uses them.
强化学习还有调度问题：生成阶段产出采样轨迹，训练阶段使用它们。

59
00:05:53,522 --> 00:05:56,530
Asynchronous rollouts sound relevant there.
异步采样轨迹在这里似乎很有用。

60
00:05:56,530 --> 00:06:03,598
I'd still evaluate how that arrangement behaves for the model and resources a team actually has.
但我仍会评估这种安排在团队实际使用的模型和资源上表现如何。

61
00:06:03,598 --> 00:06:12,148
Brian: The update also covers performance improvements, FlexShard, graph-based training, distributed communication, and checkpointing.
Brian：这次更新还涉及性能优化、FlexShard、基于计算图的训练、分布式通信和检查点。

62
00:06:12,148 --> 00:06:18,812
Those are useful areas to examine, but naming them doesn't rank their effect on a particular model.
这些都值得研究，但光列出名称无法判断它们对特定模型的影响大小。

63
00:06:18,812 --> 00:06:25,356
A team would need measurements from its own training and generation setup to make that call.
团队需要测量自己的训练和生成环境，才能做出判断。

64
00:06:25,356 --> 00:06:28,761
Ava: Here's where that matters at the kernel level.
Ava：在内核层面，这一点就很关键了。

65
00:06:28,761 --> 00:06:35,572
A developer may tune tile sizes and warp counts, while the compiler has controls of its own.
开发者可以调整分块大小和 warp 数量，编译器也有自己的控制选项。

66
00:06:35,572 --> 00:06:45,842
Helion's integration with NVIDIA CompileIQ adds Advanced Control Files to the autotuning search alongside those kernel configurations.
Helion 集成 NVIDIA CompileIQ 后，自动调优会将高级控制文件（Advanced Control Files）与这些内核配置一同纳入搜索。

67
00:06:45,842 --> 00:06:50,455
Brian: Developers can tune offline and pin the selected configuration.
Brian：开发者可以离线调优，再固定选定的配置。

68
00:06:50,455 --> 00:06:54,189
Compiler defaults remain a candidate in the search.
编译器默认配置也仍是候选项。

69
00:06:54,189 --> 00:07:02,316
That gives a developer a concrete tuning workflow: compare the available choices, then retain the selected one.
这样就有了明确的调优流程：比较各个选项，再保留选中的配置。

70
00:07:02,316 --> 00:07:09,256
The result of that search still belongs to the kernels and configurations being evaluated.
搜索结果仍只适用于所评估的内核和配置。

71
00:07:09,256 --> 00:07:14,680
Ava: So I'd keep the default in the search and inspect what the tuning run selects.
Ava：所以我会把默认配置留在候选项中，看看调优最终选了什么。

72
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:22,328
A pinned configuration is useful for that workload, but I wouldn't assume it gives every kernel the same gain.
固定配置对该任务有用，但不能假设每个内核都能获得同样的收益。

73
00:07:22,328 --> 00:07:27,198
Shapes and compiler choices are part of the engineering question.
输入形状和编译器选项也是工程上需要考虑的因素。

74
00:07:27,198 --> 00:07:32,026
Brian: Deployment brings a different device target into view.
Brian：部署时，还要考虑另一类目标设备。

75
00:07:32,026 --> 00:07:41,325
ExecuTorch now provides a direct path from PyTorch training to on-device inference on Arm Cortex-M CPUs.
ExecuTorch 现在提供了一条从 PyTorch 训练直接走向 Arm Cortex-M CPU 端侧推理的路径。

76
00:07:41,325 --> 00:07:53,924
Its Cortex-M backend uses Arm CMSIS-NN acceleration and supports the Scalar, DSP, and MVE/Helium capability tiers from a single workflow.
其 Cortex-M 后端采用 Arm CMSIS-NN 加速，并通过同一流程支持 Scalar、DSP 和 MVE/Helium 三个能力层级。

77
00:07:53,924 --> 00:08:00,140
Ava: For a team shipping to those CPUs, one workflow across the capability tiers sounds useful.
Ava：对要部署到这些 CPU 的团队来说，用一套流程覆盖各能力层级很有用。

78
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:03,869
I'd still check which tier the target device provides.
但我仍会确认目标设备支持哪个层级。

79
00:08:03,869 --> 00:08:14,026
The workflow connects training and on-device inference, while the available acceleration depends on the device the model will actually run on.
这套流程衔接了训练和端侧推理，而可用的加速能力取决于模型实际运行的设备。

80
00:08:14,026 --> 00:08:17,322
Brian: Data loading has its own portability problem.
Brian：数据加载也有自身的可移植性问题。

81
00:08:17,322 --> 00:08:21,423
A distributed job may resume with a different GPU count.
分布式任务恢复运行时，GPU 数量可能会变化。

82
00:08:21,423 --> 00:08:27,942
If its global batches change, comparing the resumed run with the original becomes harder.
如果全局批次也随之改变，就更难比较恢复后的运行与原始运行。

83
00:08:27,942 --> 00:08:35,616
Zephon's TorchTitan integration is designed to preserve identical global batches across that change.
Zephon 与 TorchTitan 的集成旨在 GPU 数量变化时保持全局批次完全一致。

84
00:08:35,616 --> 00:08:39,685
Ava: What can we actually conclude from the test?
Ava：这项测试究竟能证明什么？

85
00:08:39,685 --> 00:08:46,715
A 1B-parameter model resumed from a 16-GPU checkpoint on 8, 32, and 64 GPUs.
一个 10 亿参数模型从 16 张 GPU 的检查点恢复后，分别在 8、32 和 64 张 GPU 上运行。

86
00:08:46,715 --> 00:08:52,634
The SHA-256 hash of every global batch matched the original run.
每个全局批次的 SHA-256 哈希都与原始运行一致。

87
00:08:52,634 --> 00:08:58,718
That's a direct check of batch identity in those resumed runs.
这直接验证了这些恢复运行中的批次一致性。

88
00:08:58,718 --> 00:09:03,493
Brian: The hash result supports the global-batch claim in that test.
Brian：哈希结果支持这项测试中的全局批次一致性结论。

89
00:09:03,493 --> 00:09:08,972
By itself, it doesn't establish that every model update was identical.
但仅凭这一点，无法证明每次模型参数更新都完全相同。

90
00:09:08,972 --> 00:09:15,155
Zephon also tokenizes, packs, shuffles, and mixes data inside the training job.
Zephon 还在训练任务中完成数据的分词、打包、打乱和混合。

91
00:09:15,155 --> 00:09:19,732
That avoids keeping a preprocessed copy of the corpus.
这样就不必保留一份预处理后的语料副本。

92
00:09:19,732 --> 00:09:23,529
Ava: There's a production feedback loop in the Shopify case.
Ava：Shopify 的案例展示了一个生产反馈循环。

93
00:09:23,529 --> 00:09:32,019
Shopify uses PyTorch and vLLM in a continual learning loop that puts production failures back into model weights every day.
Shopify 用 PyTorch 和 vLLM 构建持续学习循环，每天把生产环境中的失败案例用于更新模型权重。

94
00:09:32,019 --> 00:09:41,274
That's a concrete connection between serving behavior and repeated model improvement, rather than a hardware portability example.
这是服务表现与持续改进模型之间的具体联系，而非硬件可移植性的例子。

95
00:09:41,274 --> 00:09:47,647
Brian: The conference report says Shopify beat frontier-model quality and cut serving costs by 96%.
Brian：会议报告称，Shopify 的质量超过了前沿模型，服务成本降低了 96%。

96
00:09:47,647 --> 00:09:50,279
Those are Shopify's reported outcomes.
这些是 Shopify 报告的结果。

97
00:09:50,279 --> 00:10:02,336
Before applying that number to another service, we'd need to examine its comparison setup and quality measure, then see whether the other service has similar conditions.
要把这个数字用于其他服务，得先看它的对比方式和质量指标，再判断其他服务是否具备类似条件。

98
00:10:02,336 --> 00:10:10,779
Ava: These paths cross several PyTorch Foundation projects: PyTorch, vLLM, DeepSpeed, Ray, Helion, and Safetensors.
Ava：这些路径涉及多个 PyTorch 基金会项目：PyTorch、vLLM、DeepSpeed、Ray、Helion 和 Safetensors。

99
00:10:10,779 --> 00:10:18,454
The conference theme makes more sense when you see those projects as parts of a connected ecosystem.
把这些项目看作相互连接的生态组成部分，大会主题就更容易理解了。

100
00:10:18,454 --> 00:10:26,326
Their interfaces and contributors help ideas move between training, inference, and infrastructure.
它们的接口和贡献者帮助新思路在训练、推理和基础设施之间流转。

101
00:10:26,326 --> 00:10:33,594
Brian: The Foundation announced nine new members, including Platinum members Nebius, Nscale, and Shopify.
Brian：基金会宣布新增九名成员，包括白金会员 Nebius、Nscale 和 Shopify。

102
00:10:33,594 --> 00:10:39,231
The event also had more than 100 technical sessions and 144 poster sessions.
大会还举办了 100 多场技术专题会议和 144 场海报展示。

103
00:10:39,231 --> 00:10:50,484
Those numbers show the breadth of participation, with work spanning the core framework, kernels, training, on-device inference, and responsible AI.
这些数字体现了参与面的广度，研究涵盖核心框架、算子内核、训练、端侧推理和负责任的人工智能。

104
00:10:50,484 --> 00:10:52,442
Ava: My takeaways are practical.
Ava：我的收获更偏重实操。

105
00:10:52,442 --> 00:10:59,113
For a new backend, I'd check support, then measure my workload with its shapes and sharding.
对于新后端，我会先确认支持情况，再按实际数据形状和分片方式测量工作负载。

106
00:10:59,113 --> 00:11:03,246
For a resumed training run, I'd check the global batches.
对于恢复运行的训练任务，我会检查全局批次。

107
00:11:03,246 --> 00:11:11,210
And I'd read a production result like Shopify's as a case to investigate before forecasting my own costs.
至于 Shopify 这样的生产环境成果，我会先研究具体案例，再预测自己的成本。

108
00:11:11,210 --> 00:11:23,236
Brian: That brings the announcements together: more places to run PyTorch workloads, more ways to tune them, and specific evidence to examine for each claim.
